round 9 points, though the race has tightened", "Minnesota's modest Democratic lean and strong expert ratings favoring Democrats", "$10 million outside spending boost for Demuth could narrow the gap further"], "rationale": "Polls consistently show Klobuchar ahead by high single to double digits, and markets price her near 95%, but the most recent surveys show tightening and Demuth has gained outside financial backing. A Likely Democratic rating with a mid-single-to-high-single-digit margin balances the strong polling record against late momentum risk.", "watch": "Whether Demuth's new outside money and debate performances sustain the tightening seen in mid-September polls.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tim Walz (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's open governor's race features Senator Amy Klobuchar, a well-funded Democrat with statewide name recognition, against state Representative Lisa Demuth, the Republican nominee. Klobuchar has raised roughly $7 million to Demuth's $360,000, though a Demuth-aligned PAC recently received a $10 million infusion for advertising.\n\nPolling through mid-September shows Klobuchar leading by margins ranging from 2 to 13 points, with recent surveys suggesting the race has narrowed somewhat. Expert raters uniformly place the race on the Democratic side of the ledger, and prediction markets price Klobuchar's chances around 92 to 95 percent. Minnesota's slight Democratic lean and the absence of incumbent Tim Walz on the ballot frame a contest that remains Klobuchar's to lose, with Demuth needing outside spending and debates to shift the trajectory.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 10.03}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9647, "margin": 9.5}]}